@@ -0,0 +1,270 @@
+# Inkling-Small support in WASTE
+
+Status: **source audit and deterministic conversion-plan gate implemented;
+payload conversion and C runtime are not yet implemented.**
+
+Inkling-Small was released on 2026-07-30. This document uses only the official
+release assets and the official Apache-2.0 Transformers implementation as
+architecture sources:
+
+- `thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small/config.json`
+- `thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small/model.safetensors.index.json`
+- `thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small/processor_config.json`
+- `thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small/tokenizer_config.json`
+- `thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small/chat_template.jinja`
+- `transformers/models/inkling/*`
+- the official Transformers checkpoint-conversion mapping for
+  `inkling_mm_model`
+
+No value from the larger Inkling model is used as an Inkling-Small default.
+
+## 1. Executive assessment
+
+WASTE's resident-trunk plus streamed-expert-bank design is a good fit for
+Inkling-Small. The 40 sparse layers each have 256 routed experts, while six are
+active per token. The two shared experts in every sparse layer are always
+active and therefore belong in the resident trunk, not the streamed bank.
+
+The existing WEXP record can continue to hold one expert's gate, up, and down
+matrices after the official fused `w13` layout is deterministically reordered
+and split. The expert cache, aligned `pread`, CRC validation, chunk-level expert
+deduplication, and bounded cache policy can be reused.
+
+The current C forward pass cannot execute Inkling-Small. Inkling attention is
+neither KDA nor MLA and requires:
+
+- local/global grouped-query attention;
+- per-head Q/K RMS normalization;
+- a learned hidden-state-conditioned relative-logit projection;
+- attention scale `1 / head_dim`, not `1 / sqrt(head_dim)`;
+- four depthwise causal short-convolution states per layer;
+- global-layer query and relative-bias log scaling;
+- exact routed-plus-shared expert normalization.
+
+Patch 2 therefore stops at a deterministic, shape-checked conversion plan. It
+does not create `manifest.json`, `trunk.bin`, expert banks, or codebooks.
+
+## 2. Confirmed Inkling-Small architecture mapping
+
+| Field | Value | Provenance |
+|---|---:|---|
+| architecture | `InklingForConditionalGeneration` / `inkling_mm_model` | confirmed from config |
+| source numerics | BF16 release; separate NVFP4 release | confirmed from release files |
+| hidden size | 4096 | confirmed from config |
+| decoder layers | 42 | confirmed from config |
+| configured maximum context | 1,048,576 | confirmed from config |
+| vocabulary rows | 201,024 | confirmed from config |
+| unembed rows | 200,058 | confirmed from config |
+| dense MLP layers | 0-1 | confirmed from `dense_mlp_idx=2` |
+| sparse MLP layers | 2-41 | derived from config |
+| dense intermediate | 16,384 | confirmed from config |
+| routed intermediate | 2,048 | confirmed from config |
+| routed experts | 256 | confirmed from config |
+| routed top-k | 6 | confirmed from config |
+| shared experts | 2 | confirmed from config |
+| router activation | sigmoid | confirmed from config and code |
+| route scale | 8.0 | confirmed from config |
+| router correction bias | one value per routed expert | confirmed from index and code |
+| global Q/KV heads | 32 / 8 | confirmed from config |
+| local Q/KV heads | 32 / 8 | confirmed from config |
+| head dimension | 128 | confirmed from config |
+| local window | 512 | confirmed from config |
+| local layers | 0-4, 6-10, 12-16, 18-22, 24-28, 30-34, 36-40 | confirmed from config |
+| global layers | 5, 11, 17, 23, 29, 35, 41 | complement of config local IDs |
+| relative state dimension | 16 | confirmed from config |
+| global relative extent | 1,024 | confirmed from config |
+| local relative extent | 512 | confirmed from official code |
+| short-convolution kernel | 4 | confirmed from config |
+| convolution states | K, V, attention output, MLP output | confirmed from official code |
+| EOS | 200006 | confirmed from config |
+| image placeholder | `<|unused_200054|>` -> 200054 | processor plus tokenizer metadata |
+| audio placeholder | `<|unused_200053|>` -> 200053 | processor plus tokenizer metadata |
+| image BOS | `<|content_image|>` -> 200005 | processor plus tokenizer metadata |
+| audio BOS | `<|content_audio_input|>` -> 200020 | processor plus tokenizer metadata |
+| vision | hMLP, patch 40, temporal patch 2, RGB, four linear stages | confirmed from config/index |
+| audio | 16 kHz, 80 mel bands, 50 ms hop, 1,600-point FFT, 16 dMel bins | processor/config |
+| prompt format | official `chat_template.jinja` | official sidecar |
+
+### Exact text source grammar
+
+The official BF16 source uses provider-raw names:
+
+- core: `model.llm.embed`, `embed_norm`, `norm`, `unembed`;
+- attention: `wq_du`, `wk_dv`, `wv_dv`, `wr_du`, `wo_ud`, Q/K norms,
+  relative-logit projection, K/V short convolutions;
+- residual short convolutions: `attn_sconv`, `mlp_sconv`;
+- dense MLP: `w13_dn`, `w2_md`, `global_scale`;
+- sparse MLP: `experts.w13_weight`, `experts.w2_weight`, router weight,
+  correction bias, router global scale, and shared-expert fused weights.
+
+The official Transformers conversion mapping establishes these transformations:
+
+- dense `w13_dn`: interleave axis 0, then split axis 0 into gate/up;
+- routed `experts.w13_weight`: interleave axis 1 into grouped gate/up;
+- shared `shared_w13_weight`: interleave axis 1, then split axis 1;
+- attention projections and short-convolution weights: rename without a
+  transpose;
+- MTP tensors: ignored by the base model and excluded from baseline parity.
+
+Patch 2 encodes and shape-checks those transformations but does not read tensor
+payload bytes.
+
+## 3. Remaining blockers
+
+### Blocking payload conversion
+
+- A local BF16 checkpoint must include all 32 required shards. The index alone
+  is sufficient for audit but not conversion.
+- Every required tensor header must expose the expected shape and dtype.
+- The payload writer must split fused expert weights without holding more than
+  one routed expert or one bounded source slice in RAM.
+- The proposed manifest extension must be accepted only by an Inkling-aware
+  loader; the current Kimi loader must never interpret it.
+- Expert-bank round-trip, resume, index, CRC, and shape tests must pass.
+
+### Blocking text inference parity
+
+- `WASTE_ARCH_INKLING` and fail-closed architecture dispatch.
+- Per-layer local/global KV caches and four convolution rings.
+- Relative-logit attention and exact global scaling.
+- Dense MLP global scaling.
+- Exact router/shared-expert equations.
+- Layerwise BF16 differential tests against the official Python implementation.
+- Final-logit tolerance documented before any WASTE quantization is enabled.
+
+### Deferred, not blocking text-only parity
+
+- Vision hMLP and exact patch construction.
+- Audio STFT, Slaney mel bank, log10 and dMel quantization.
+- Multimodal placeholder expansion.
+- OpenAI-compatible image/audio request handling.
+- MTP heads.
+- NVFP4 source conversion.
+
+## 4. Compatibility matrix
+
+| Area | Classification | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| aligned expert records and CRC | already generic | reuse |
+| streamed banks and bounded expert cache | already generic | reuse |
+| trunk tensor registry and quantized matmul | already generic | reuse with Inkling names |
+| raw completion API | already generic | preserve |
+| architecture detection | parameterized in patch 1 | explicit Inkling identifiers only |
+| source inventory and provenance | implemented | provider-raw and normalized dialects |
+| nested tokenizer discovery | implemented | includes `tiktoken/tokenizer.model` |
+| exact processor token-ID resolution | implemented in patch 2 | no token-name guessing |
+| payload availability gate | implemented in patch 2 | index-only and local-shard readiness separated |
+| deterministic conversion plan | implemented in patch 2 | 42 layer descriptors and 40 banks |
+| fused `w13` payload conversion | needs implementation | next converter patch |
+| shared experts | plan complete; runtime absent | resident trunk |
+| hybrid attention | needs C implementation | new module |
+| router | needs C implementation | new equations |
+| vision | needs new implementation | existing K3 tower is incompatible |
+| audio | needs new implementation | new dependency-free C path |
+| serving | needs parameterization | official template only |
+
+## 5. Implemented milestone order
+
+### Patch 1 — completed
+
+- `tools/inkling_source.py`: explicit architecture identification.
+- `tools/inspect_inkling.py`: config/index/tensor/sidecar audit.
+- `tools/convert.py`: fail closed before the Kimi conversion path.
+- synthetic inventory tests.
+
+### Patch 2 — completed
+
+- distinguishes metadata readiness from local payload/header readiness;
+- resolves media token IDs from official tokenizer metadata;
+- adds exact official-Small dimensions and schedule tests;
+- adds `tools/inkling_plan.py`:
+  - exact layer descriptors;
+  - shape probes derived from official config and code;
+  - resident trunk inventory;
+  - streamed routed-expert bank inventory;
+  - explicit MTP/vision/audio exclusions;
+  - manifest preview that is never published as a container;
+- adds `tools/convert_inkling.py --plan-only`;
+- refuses normal conversion and leaves no partial output.
+
+### Patch 3 — next
+
+Implement the BF16 text payload writer:
+
+1. Open source shards lazily and read bounded tensor slices.
+2. Copy/quantize the resident trunk with exact shape checks.
+3. Reorder/split dense and shared fused `w13` tensors.
+4. Convert one routed expert at a time into existing WEXP records.
+5. Keep shared experts resident.
+6. Exclude MTP, vision and audio from the text-only container.
+7. Copy official tokenizer and template sidecars verbatim.
+8. Verify the staging tree, then publish `manifest.json` last.
+
+The initial correctness build should support unquantized or loss-minimized BF16
+fixtures before VQ/Q4/Q8 production conversion is enabled.
+
+### Patch 4 — C text runtime
+
+- add architecture enum and Inkling config structs;
+- parse per-layer descriptors;
+- implement local/global attention, convolution state and caches;
+- implement dense and sparse MLPs and shared-expert routing;
+- preserve WASTE's expert cache and direct-I/O path;
+- add layerwise debug dumps and Python differential harness.
+
+### Patches 5-8
+
+Tokenizer/chat integration, vision, audio, then OpenAI-compatible serving.
+
+## 6. Tests
+
+Patch 2 adds deterministic tests for:
+
+- explicit architecture detection;
+- official source grammar and nested tokenizer path;
+- official processor token strings resolving to exact IDs;
+- index-only versus payload-ready checkpoints;
+- missing required sparse tensors;
+- MTP and quantized-source deferral;
+- raw mode when no official template exists;
+- exact Small dimensions and global-layer schedule;
+- all conversion-plan shape probes;
+- shared experts resident and routed experts streamed;
+- mismatch rejection before conversion;
+- plan-only output containing no container commit files.
+
+Run:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m py_compile \
+  tools/inkling_source.py \
+  tools/inspect_inkling.py \
+  tools/inkling_plan.py \
+  tools/convert_inkling.py \
+  tests/test_inspect_inkling.py \
+  tests/test_inkling_plan.py \
+  tests/test_convert_inkling.py
+
+PYTHONPATH=tools:tests python3 -m unittest discover \
+  -s tests -p 'test_*inkling*.py' -v
+```
+
+## 7. Risks and fallback paths
+
+- **Header shape differs from the official code-derived shape:** stop. Update the
+  mapping from the actual official header and explain the release difference;
+  never transpose until a mismatch “goes away.”
+- **BF16 download is incomplete:** permit index-only planning, but require all
+  base-text shards for conversion.
+- **Context memory exceeds the user's budget:** make load-time context capacity
+  explicit. Never claim unconditional one-million-token operation.
+- **Top-6 read amplification:** benchmark only after parity. First reuse chunked
+  prefill and expert deduplication; then evaluate read-ahead/cache tuning.
+- **Shared-expert cost:** keep both experts resident and separate until exact
+  parity; fuse only after differential tests.
+- **Template incompatibility:** preserve raw mode and report it. Never synthesize
+  a template.
+- **Multimodal dependencies:** port preprocessing to dependency-free C from
+  official equations and fixtures; defer rather than add a runtime framework.
+- **License:** new WASTE code is Apache-2.0. Source comments must identify any
+  equations ported from the official Apache-2.0 Transformers implementation.
